/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:14Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T12:02:14Z","body":"You still need to bake them on desktop, where does it say importing 3D scenes/meshes is an exception to this?\n\nBut to clarify \"breaking compatibility\" doesn't mean that it isn't compatible with some platforms, it means some change broke things that used to work before (in this case baking was turned off in 4.2, but it never really worked so that change didn't break compatibility)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2962412366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2962504451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107398#issuecomment-2962504451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107398","id":2962504451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wlDsD","user":{"login":"Mewlkor","id":116582174,"node_id":"U_kgDOBvLnHg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116582174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor","html_url":"https://github.com/Mewlkor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mewlkor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T12:31:06Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T12:31:06Z","body":"The [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/3d/global_illumination/using_lightmap_gi.html#setting-up) states, that Android and Web can only render lightmaps. It also says that .unwrap_cache files should be version controlled such that the UV2 reimports are consistent for all platforms. This means that while baking is not supported on android, you should be able to correctly import .unwrap_cache files on other platforms and render imported lightmaps. But i can not do that with meshes that stem from glTF/glb scenes. This is why i did not include a LightmapGI node in the MRP. The lightbaking is NOT the problem. The UV2 unwrapping and importing of scenes which have their import option set to uwrap UV2 is. Because this seems to not work correctly which results in an error.\nSo maybe breaking compatability is the wrong term for this, but i am not sure how to call it otherwise since english isnt my first language.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2962504451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"e